, true ),
	'en' => json_decode( <<<'JSON_EN'
{"fecha":"20261105","cierre":"<strong>How we created this page.</strong> This is our own research based on public data and partner providers. Prices are as published or reported to guests as of 5 November 2026, in the currency shown. Totals and per-day fishing prices are our calculations. Rates change: confirm them before booking. If you are an operator and your rate changed, write to us and we’ll update it.","paginas":[{"clave":"viaje-dorado-amigos-precios","slug":"golden-dorado-fishing-trip-with-friends","especie":"dorado","titulo":"Golden dorado fishing trip with friends: how many days, how much it costs, and where to stay (2026/27)","bajada":"Three ways to plan a golden dorado trip with friends on the Paraná: per-person prices for each, what's included, and how many days are best.","seo_title":"Golden dorado fishing trip with friends: 2026/27 prices","seo_description":"How much a golden dorado fishing trip with friends in Argentina costs: from US$ 605 per person at an inn to US$ 4,050 at a lodge. Days and what's included.","datos":["Inn in Esquina (Corrientes): 2 fishing days and 3 nights from US$ 605 per person in a group of three and from US$ 705 in a group of two, with meals, boat, guide, and license.","Houseboat in the Paraná Delta: 3 nights from US$ 1,260 and 4 nights from US$ 1,680 per person.","All-inclusive lodge in Corrientes: 3 nights and 2 fishing days from US$ 4,050 per person; 7 nights and 6 days US$ 7,950.","The more days, the cheaper each fishing day: at an inn in Esquina, it drops from US$ 353 to US$ 326 per person between 2 and 4 days.","The extraordinary fishing ban on the Paraná in Corrientes was lifted on 29 September 2026."],"bloques":[{"t":"p","h":"<strong>Short answer.</strong> For a dorado trip with friends, it's best to go for <strong>2 to 4 fishing days</strong>. The per-person price depends more on the type of lodging than the number of days: <strong>from US$ 605 to US$ 705</strong> at an inn (2 fishing days, 3 nights), <strong>from US$ 1,260</strong> on a Delta houseboat, and <strong>from US$ 4,050</strong> at an all-inclusive lodge. All prices are per person, in US dollars, not including travel."},{"t":"h2","h":"Three ways to do it, with prices"},{"t":"tabla","cab":["Format","Where","Nights and fishing days","From, per person","What's included"],"filas":[["<strong>Inn with package</strong>","Esquina, Corrientes","3 nights, 2 days (group of 2)","US$ 705","Lodging, meals, drinks, boat, guide, bait, fuel, and license"],["<strong>Inn with package</strong>","Esquina, Corrientes","3 nights, 2 days (group of 3)","US$ 605","Same, with the price split among three"],["<strong>Houseboat</strong>","Upper Paraná Delta","3 nights, 2 and a half days","US$ 1,260","Onboard lodging, meals, guided fishing"],["<strong>Houseboat</strong>","Upper Paraná Delta","4 nights, 3 and a half days","US$ 1,680","Same, one more day"],["<strong>All-inclusive lodge</strong>","Paraná, Corrientes","3 nights, 2 days","US$ 4,050","Double lodging, all meals and drinks, guide, and loaner gear"],["<strong>All-inclusive lodge</strong>","Paraná, Corrientes","7 nights, 6 days","US$ 7,950","Same; does not include license, transfers, or travel"]]},{"t":"p","h":"Prices published or reported as of 5 November 2026, per person in double room and shared guide. Each lodge's rates by number of nights are in <a href=\"{n:precio-viaje-dorado-lodge}\">how much a golden dorado fishing trip costs</a>."},{"t":"h2","h":"How many days are best for a dorado trip with friends?"},{"t":"p","h":"Our opinion, based on published numbers: <strong>3 nights and 2 fishing days</strong> if time is short, since a windy or rainy day matters less than on a one-day trip; and <strong>4 nights and 3 days</strong> if you're traveling from far away, as the cost per fishing day drops and travel is already paid. At an inn in Esquina, the per-person, per-fishing-day cost goes from US$ 353 (2 days) to US$ 337 (3 days) and US$ 326 (4 days), for a group of two. These are our calculations."},{"t":"h2","h":"Multi-day packages at an inn in Esquina"},{"t":"tabla","cab":["Format","Group in the boat","Per person","Per fishing day","Group total"],"filas":[["2 fishing days, 3 nights","2","US$ 705","US$ 353","US$ 1,410"],["3 fishing days, 4 nights","2","US$ 1,010","US$ 337","US$ 2,020"],["4 fishing days, 5 nights","2","US$ 1,305","US$ 326","US$ 2,610"],["2 fishing days, 3 nights","3","US$ 605","US$ 303","US$ 1,815"],["3 fishing days, 4 nights","3","US$ 855","US$ 285","US$ 2,565"],["4 fishing days, 5 nights","3","US$ 1,105","US$ 276","US$ 3,315"]]},{"t":"p","h":"Posada Hambaré, National Route 12, km 688, Esquina. \"From\" prices as of 4 November 2026; the inn does not publish the season for these rates. Includes lodging; breakfast, lunch, and dinner; soft drinks, water, beer, and unlimited wine; boat, fishing guide, two dozen live baits per person, 50 liters of fuel, and fishing license. Totals and cost per fishing day are our calculations."},{"t":"h2","h":"How much for your group?"},{"t":"tabla","cab":["Friends","How it's split","Total with published prices"],"filas":[["2","One boat, 2 days and 3 nights","US$ 1,410"],["3","One boat, 2 days and 3 nights","US$ 1,815"],["4","Two boats of 2","US$ 2,820"],["6","Two boats of 3","US$ 3,630"]]},{"t":"p","h":"Our calculation, not including travel or gear. For 4 and 6 friends, you need to confirm the inn has two boats available on your dates and that each group keeps its price."},{"t":"h2","h":"What if you prefer a one-day trip?"},{"t":"p","h":"A guide in Esquina advertises a full day on the boat with guide <strong>from $ 480,000 per boat</strong>, or $ 160,000 per person if there are three (1 November 2026, in pesos). In Paso de la Patria, none of the operators we checked publish a day rate: offers say \"all inclusive\" or \"inquire.\" We do not set the exchange rate between pesos and dollars: confirm it when booking."},{"t":"h2","h":"Is there a fishing ban on the Paraná in Corrientes now?"},{"t":"tabla","cab":["Date","What happened"],"filas":[["30 May 2026","Order 618: ban between km 1232 and 1238, due to a concentration of surubí"],["16 September 2026","Extended to km 1180 to 1239, Paso de la Patria jurisdiction, for dorado and sábalo"],["29 September 2026, 13:00","Order 1054: ban lifted and regulations from Order 853/22 reinstated"]]},{"t":"p","h":"Corrientes Department of Natural Resources. We found no ban after 4 November 2026, but the rules allow it to be reinstated if fish concentrations reappear: ask your guide before heading out. Since Order 853/22, dorado and surubí must be released in Corrientes."},{"t":"h2","h":"Do I need a fishing license?"},{"t":"p","h":"Yes. In Corrientes, you get the sport fishing license online and carry it with your ID. It's already included in Esquina inn packages and some lodges; in others, it's not (the Corrientes lodges in the nights table do not include it). Always ask."},{"t":"p","h":"<strong>Want help planning?</strong> Tell us your dates, number of friends, and budget in <a href=\"{viaje}\">the trip form</a> and we'll send you guide and lodging options, free of charge and with no obligation."},{"t":"h2","h":"What this page doesn't cover yet"},{"t":"p","h":"Bus and flight schedules from Buenos Aires, the Corrientes license price, and a month-by-month calendar with technical sources. We'll add them once we verify with a date."}]},{"clave":"precio-viaje-dorado-lodge","slug":"how-much-does-dorado-fishing-trip-cost","especie":"dorado","titulo":"How much does a dorado fishing trip in Argentina cost: all-inclusive lodges by number of nights (2026/27)","bajada":"Per person rates for dorado lodges in Corrientes, Iberá, the Paraná in Santa Fe, and the Delta, with what's included and the cost per fishing day.","seo_title":"How much does a dorado fishing trip cost (2026/27)","seo_description":"Dorado lodge prices in Argentina for 2026/27: from US$ 4,050 for 3 nights to US$ 7,950 for 7 nights, per person, with what's included and cost per day.","datos":["An all-inclusive lodge on the Upper Paraná in Corrientes costs from US$ 4,050 (3 nights, 2 fishing days) to US$ 7,950 (7 nights, 6 days) per person in double occupancy.","Each extra fishing day lowers the price per day: from US$ 2,025 with 2 days to US$ 1,325 with 6 days at the same lodge.","Iberá Wetlands: one lodge lists 7 nights and 6 days from US$ 6,400 per person, in a single room.","Paraná in Santa Fe: 4 fishing days from US$ 3,600; a special of 3 days and 4 nights at US$ 2,500 on selected dates from December 2026 to February 2027.","Fishing licenses and transfers are usually not included: add them in."],"bloques":[{"t":"p","h":"<strong>Short answer.</strong> An all-inclusive dorado trip at a lodge in Argentina costs, per person in a double room, <strong>from US$ 4,050 for 3 nights and 2 fishing days to US$ 7,950 for 7 nights and 6 days</strong> on the Upper Paraná (Corrientes). In Iberá and the Paraná in Santa Fe there are options from US$ 2,500 to US$ 6,400. For a cheaper trip, see <a href=\"{n:viaje-dorado-amigos-precios}\">the friends' trip at an inn</a> (from US$ 605)."},{"t":"h2","h":"Price ladder by number of nights (Paraná, Corrientes)"},{"t":"tabla","cab":["Nights and fishing days","Per person","Per fishing day (our calculation)"],"filas":[["3 nights, 2 days","US$ 4,050","US$ 2,025"],["4 nights, 3 days","US$ 5,350","US$ 1,783"],["5 nights, 4 days","US$ 6,495","US$ 1,624"],["6 nights, 5 days","US$ 7,595","US$ 1,519"],["7 nights, 6 days","US$ 7,950","US$ 1,325"]]},{"t":"p","h":"2026/27 rate for two Upper Paraná lodges in Corrientes (one open October 2026 to May 2027 and the other year-round), same price. Per person, double room, shared guide. Includes lodging, all meals, wine, beer and drinks, professional guide, and loaner gear (rods, reels, and lines). Does not include flights, transfers, fishing license, laundry, or tips. Single room and boat: 60% surcharge. Non-fishing companion: US$ 650 per night. Full fishing day on arrival or departure: US$ 950 per boat."},{"t":"h2","h":"Other lodges and formats"},{"t":"tabla","cab":["Where","Format","Price per person","Conditions"],"filas":[["Itatí, Corrientes (Upper Paraná)","7 nights, 6 days","US$ 7,850","Double. Includes charter flights from Buenos Aires, transfers, license, flies, and gear. 2026/27 season"],["Itatí, Corrientes (Upper Paraná)","4 nights, 3 days","US$ 4,050","Same as above"],["Iberá Wetlands, Corrientes","7 nights, 6 days","US$ 6,400","Single room and shared guide; 2-for-1 introductory rate depending on the lodge"],["Iberá Wetlands, Corrientes","7 nights, 6 days (2025 rate)","US$ 6,340","Double; includes transfer from Corrientes and license. Published rate for September to May 2025: reconfirm"],["Paraná, Santa Fe","4 fishing days","from US$ 3,600","August to April"],["Paraná, Santa Fe","3 days and 4 nights (special)","US$ 2,500","Selected dates from December 2026 to February 2027"],["Upper Paraná Delta (boat-hotel)","3 nights, 2 and a half days","from US$ 1,260","Catamaran for 8 guests"],["Upper Paraná Delta (boat-hotel)","4 nights, 3 and a half days","from US$ 1,680","Same as above"]]},{"t":"p","h":"Prices published or reported as of 5 November 2026, in US dollars, as shown by each operator. Each operator includes different things: just comparing the number can be misleading."},{"t":"h2","h":"How many days are best?"},{"t":"p","h":"The price per fishing day drops with each extra day: in the ladder above it goes from US$ 2,025 with 2 days to US$ 1,325 with 6. If budget is tight, 3 nights and 2 days is the minimum worth considering; if you're coming from far away, 5 nights and 4 days already covers a bad weather day without losing your week."},{"t":"h2","h":"What is usually not included in the price?"},{"t":"lista","items":["<strong>The fishing license</strong>: in Corrientes you get it online; some lodges include it, others don't.","<strong>Flights and transfers</strong> to the lodge, unless listed as included.","<strong>Tips</strong> for guides and staff.","<strong>Single supplement</strong>: if you travel alone and want your own room and boat, the surcharge can be up to 60%."]},{"t":"p","h":"<strong>Want to compare for your dates and group?</strong> Write to us on <a href=\"{viaje}\">the trip form</a> and we'll send you options, no cost or obligation."}]},{"clave":"precio-pesca-bariloche-limay","slug":"how-much-does-fly-fishing-bariloche-cost","especie":"trucha","titulo":"How much does a day of fly fishing cost in Bariloche and the Limay River (2026/27)","bajada":"Price for a guided fishing day on the Limay River: in US dollars and pesos, what's included, license cost, and what changes if there are two anglers.","seo_title":"How much is fishing in Bariloche & Limay (2026/27)","seo_description":"Day rates for guided fly fishing on the Limay River, Bariloche: from US$ 500 to US$ 545 per boat in dollars and from $ 666,000 in pesos. What's included.","datos":["A full day of guided fly fishing on the Limay with boat costs between US$ 500 and US$ 545 (one angler), depending on the outfitter.","For two anglers in the same boat, one outfitter lists US$ 520: the second angler adds only US$ 20.","In pesos, a guide on a booking platform lists $ 666,000 per day for up to two people (March 2027).","The fishing license is usually not included. Official rates 2026/27, in pesos: foreigners $ 50,000 per day, $ 140,000 for 10 days, and $ 280,000 for the season; residents $ 12,500, $ 25,000, and $ 50,000.","The best season according to one outfitter is from November to May."],"bloques":[{"t":"p","h":"<strong>Short answer.</strong> A full day of guided fly fishing on the Limay River, about 45 minutes from Bariloche, costs <strong>between US$ 500 and US$ 545 per boat</strong>, and <strong>$ 666,000</strong> in pesos on a booking platform (up to two people). The fishing license is almost always paid separately."},{"t":"h2","h":"Day rates on the Limay River"},{"t":"tabla","cab":["Operator (type)","Duration","Price","Includes","Not included"],"filas":[["Fly fishing guide (local outfitter)","Full day, 8 to 10 hours","US$ 500 one angler; US$ 520 two anglers","Boat, fishing gear, Patagonian lunch with wine, soft drinks, beer, and transfers","Fishing license and tips"],["Limay fishing experience (Bariloche agency)","Half day or full day","From US$ 545","Boat for up to 2 people, transfer from Bariloche hotels, bilingual guide, full gear, snack or lunch with drinks","License, tips, and flights"],["Guide on booking platform","9 hours (08:00 to 17:00), up to 2 people","$ 666,000 per day (March 2027)","Guide, boat, lunch, gear, and transfers","License and tips"]]},{"t":"p","h":"Rates published or reported as of 5 November 2026. Dollar and peso prices are from different operators and are not converted between each other: each sets their own exchange rate at booking."},{"t":"h2","h":"How much for two anglers?"},{"t":"p","h":"With the outfitter that lists both rates, <strong>one angler pays US$ 500 and two anglers in the same boat pay US$ 520 total</strong>: the second angler adds only US$ 20. Per person, going as a pair is almost half price (our calculation: US$ 260 per person)."},{"t":"h2","h":"How much is the fishing license?"},{"t":"p","h":"The Patagonian permit is valid in Neuquén, Río Negro, Chubut, and National Parks, and the 2026/27 rates are official, in pesos: <strong>non-resident foreigners, $ 50,000 per day, $ 140,000 for 10 days, and $ 280,000 for the season; residents, $ 12,500, $ 25,000, and $ 50,000</strong> (regulations updated 26 October 2026). All rates, who is exempt, and which extra permit is needed for trolling are in <a href=\"{n:licencia-pesca-patagonia-precios}\">Patagonia fishing license 2026/27</a>."},{"t":"h2","h":"When is the best time to go?"},{"t":"p","h":"A local outfitter suggests the best season is from November to May. This is one outfitter's description; the official season and closures are in our <a href=\"{n:cuando-pescar-trucha-patagonia}\">Patagonia trout season guide</a>."},{"t":"h2","h":"<strong>Want help choosing?</strong> Tell us your dates and group size in <a href=\"{viaje}\">the trip form</a> and we'll reply with guide options, no cost or obligation."}]},{"clave":"precio-semana-trucha-patagonia-norte","slug":"how-much-does-a-week-trout-fishing-patagonia-cost","especie":"trucha","titulo":"How much does a week of trout fishing cost in Neuquén and Chubut: all-inclusive lodges (2026/27)","bajada":"Per person rates for trout lodges in Junín de los Andes, Cholila, Futaleufú, and Trevelin: 3 to 7 nights, with what's included at each.","seo_title":"How much is a week of trout fishing (2026/27)","seo_description":"Price for a week of fly fishing at lodges in Neuquén and Chubut in 2026/27: from US$ 3,950 for 3 nights to US$ 9,200 for 7 nights, per person.","datos":["A lodge on the Chimehuín River (Junín de los Andes, Neuquén) costs from US$ 3,950 (3 nights, 2 fishing days) to US$ 6,950 (7 nights, 6 days) per person, from December 2026 to April 2027.","A lodge chain in Chubut lists 7 nights and 6 fishing days from US$ 6,545 (Trevelin) up to US$ 9,200 (Cholila), in high season.","A hosted week in Trevelin, from 6 to 13 March 2027, costs US$ 5,800 per angler and includes licenses and transfers from Esquel.","These prices are per person in double occupancy and with shared guide."],"bloques":[{"t":"p","h":"<strong>Short answer.</strong> A week of fly fishing at an all-inclusive lodge in Argentine Patagonia costs, per person in double occupancy, <strong>from US$ 5,800 to US$ 9,200 for 7 nights and 6 fishing days</strong>. In Neuquén, a Chimehuín lodge lists the full range, <strong>from US$ 3,950 for 3 nights to US$ 6,950 for 7</strong>."},{"t":"h2","h":"Neuquén: price breakdown by nights (Chimehuín River, Junín de los Andes)"},{"t":"tabla","cab":["Nights and fishing days","Per person","Per fishing day (our calculation)"],"filas":[["3 nights, 2 days","US$ 3,950","US$ 1,975"],["4 nights, 3 days","US$ 4,950","US$ 1,650"],["5 nights, 4 days","US$ 5,750","US$ 1,438"],["6 nights, 5 days","US$ 6,350","US$ 1,270"],["7 nights, 6 days","US$ 6,950","US$ 1,158"]]},{"t":"p","h":"Rates from December 2026 to April 2027, per person, in double occupancy and with shared guide. The official season opens on 1 November, but this lodge usually opens its doors on 1 December."},{"t":"h2","h":"Chubut: 7-night, 6-day week (Cholila, Futaleufú, and Trevelin)"},{"t":"tabla","cab":["Lodge","Area","Per person, high season","Conditions"],"filas":[["Cholila Lodge","Lake Cholila, Chubut","US$ 9,200","All-inclusive, double, shared guide"],["Futaleufú Lodge","Futaleufú, Chubut","US$ 8,750","All-inclusive, double, shared guide"],["Trevelin Lodge","Trevelin, Chubut","US$ 6,545","All-inclusive, double, shared guide"],["Hosted week in Trevelin","Futaleufú River, 6 to 13 March 2027","US$ 5,800","7 nights, 6 fishing days, meals, drinks, transfers from Esquel and licenses"]]},{"t":"p","h":"Prices published or reported as of 5 November 2026. The lodge chain offers weeks from Saturday to Saturday; prices vary by date and some lodges accept stays of other lengths. Includes lodging, meals, drinks, and guide. License is not included unless stated by the operator (the Trevelin week does include it) and flights are confirmed with each operator. Official license rates at <a href=\"{n:licencia-pesca-patagonia-precios}\">Patagonia fishing license 2026/27</a>."},{"t":"h2","h":"How many days are best?"},{"t":"p","h":"At the Neuquén lodge with the full range, each extra fishing day lowers the per-day price: from US$ 1,975 with 2 days to US$ 1,158 with 6. A 4-night, 3-day stay is the shortest that justifies the trip; a full week makes the most of the travel."},{"t":"h2","h":"When is the season?"},{"t":"p","h":"Each province sets its own dates. The ones we've checked, with sources, are in <a href=\"{n:cuando-pescar-trucha-patagonia}\">our season article</a> and in the <a href=\"{calendario}\">fishing calendar</a>."},{"t":"p","h":"<strong>Want help choosing a lodge?</strong> Write to us using <a href=\"{viaje}\">the trip form</a> and we'll send you options for your dates, with no cost or obligation."}]},{"clave":"precio-pesca-patagonia-sur","slug":"how-much-does-it-cost-to-fish-tierra-del-fuego-calafate","especie":"trucha","titulo":"How much does it cost to fish in Tierra del Fuego and El Calafate: sea-run trout and day trips (2026/27)","bajada":"The price of a week of sea-run trout at a Río Grande lodge and a half-day or full-day trip in El Calafate, with what each includes.","seo_title":"How much does it cost to fish Tierra del Fuego & Calafate","seo_description":"Fishing prices in southern Patagonia: a week of sea-run trout in Río Grande from US$ 12,950 and a day trip in El Calafate from $ 440,000.","datos":["A week at a sea-run trout lodge in Río Grande (Tierra del Fuego) costs from US$ 12,950 to US$ 14,950 per person, depending on the date, in the 2026/27 season.","That lodge rate is for a single room and shared guide, and includes meals, drinks, and transfer from the airport.","In El Calafate, a half-day trip (5 hours) costs $ 440,000 per angler and a full-day trip (9 hours) $ 720,000.","In El Calafate, fishing is from the shore, wading; non-fishing companions pay $ 185,000 for half-day and $ 335,000 for full-day."],"bloques":[{"t":"p","h":"<strong>Short answer.</strong> In southern Patagonia there are two published price points. A <strong>week of sea-run trout at a Río Grande lodge</strong> (Tierra del Fuego) costs <strong>from US$ 12,950 to US$ 14,950 per person</strong>. A <strong>day trip in El Calafate</strong> costs <strong>$ 440,000 (half-day) or $ 720,000 (full-day) per angler</strong>, in pesos."},{"t":"h2","h":"Sea-run trout in Río Grande: week at a lodge"},{"t":"tabla","cab":["Week","Per person","Conditions"],"filas":[["26 December to 9 January","US$ 13,950","Single room, shared guide"],["9 January to 20 March","US$ 14,950","Single room, shared guide"],["20 March to 17 April","US$ 12,950","Single room, shared guide"]]},{"t":"p","h":"Río Grande lodge rate for the season from 26 December 2026 to 17 April 2027, checked on 4 November 2026. Includes lodging, transfer from Río Grande airport, all meals and drinks, professional guide (two anglers per guide), and loaner gear. Does not include flights, fishing license (the lodge estimates about US$ 550 per angler), laundry, or tips. A 50% deposit is required and is non-refundable. Other operators we found in Río Grande do not publish rates; the destination guide is at <a href=\"{n:rio-grande}\">fishing in Río Grande</a>."},{"t":"h2","h":"El Calafate: half-day or full-day trip"},{"t":"tabla","cab":["Trip","Angler","Non-fishing companion"],"filas":[["Half-day (5 hours)","$ 440,000","$ 185,000"],["Full-day (9 hours)","$ 720,000","$ 335,000"]]},{"t":"p","h":"Prices in pesos published by an El Calafate agency, as of 5 November 2026. Includes transfer from the hotel, fishing guide, full fly or spinning gear, drinks, hot beverages, insurance, and fishing permits. Fishing is catch and release, from the shore, wading; no boat fishing. Locations are about 50 minutes from El Calafate and are chosen the same day based on weather and water levels."},{"t":"h2","h":"What extra costs should you expect?"},{"t":"lista","items":["<strong>Flights</strong> to Río Grande or El Calafate: lodge rates start at the airport.","<strong>Fishing license</strong> in Tierra del Fuego: the lodge estimates about US$ 550 per angler per week.","<strong>Tips</strong> for guides and staff."]},{"t":"p","h":"<strong>Want to compare with other destinations?</strong> See how much a <a href=\"{n:precio-semana-trucha-patagonia-norte}\">week of trout fishing in Neuquén and Chubut</a> costs, or write to us in <a href=\"{viaje}\">the trip form</a>."}]},{"clave":"licencia-pesca-patagonia-precios","slug":"patagonia-fishing-license-2026-27","especie":"trucha","titulo":"Patagonia Argentina Fishing License 2026/27: Cost and Validity","bajada":"Official rates for the Patagonian fishing permit for the 2026/27 season, for foreigners and residents, where it is valid, how long it lasts, and what is charged separately.","seo_title":"Patagonia fishing license 2026/27: prices","seo_description":"How much is the Patagonia fishing permit 2026/27: foreigners ARS 50,000 per day and ARS 280,000 per season; residents from ARS 12,500. Where it is valid.","datos":["Non-resident foreigners: ARS 50,000 per day, ARS 140,000 for 10 days, and ARS 280,000 for the season (2026/27 rates, in pesos).","Residents in Argentina: ARS 12,500 per day, ARS 25,000 for 10 days, and ARS 50,000 for the season.","The same permit is valid in Neuquén, Río Negro, Chubut, and the Southern National Parks; Santa Cruz and Tierra del Fuego have their own.","The fishing season runs from 1 November 2026 to 1 May 2027 inclusive; the season permit is valid until 31 October 2027.","No charge: people over 65, retirees, pensioners, children up to 12 years old, and people with disabilities with official accreditation."],"bloques":[{"t":"p","h":"<strong>Short answer.</strong> To fish in Argentine Patagonia in the 2026/27 season, a <strong>non-resident foreigner pays ARS 50,000 for one day, ARS 140,000 for 10 days, or ARS 280,000 for the season</strong>, and a resident pays <strong>ARS 12,500, ARS 25,000, or ARS 50,000</strong>. The permit is the same in Neuquén, Río Negro, Chubut, and the Southern National Parks."},{"t":"h2","h":"Permit rates 2026/27"},{"t":"tabla","cab":["Category","One day","10 days","Season"],"filas":[["<strong>Non-resident foreigner</strong>","ARS 50,000","ARS 140,000","ARS 280,000"],["<strong>Resident in Argentina</strong> (Argentine citizens and resident foreigners)","ARS 12,500","ARS 25,000","ARS 50,000"],["Resident aged 13 to 17","","","ARS 25,000"],["Trolling (additional permit, in addition to the regular one)","ARS 25,000","ARS 50,000","ARS 100,000"]]},{"t":"p","h":"Rates in Argentine pesos from the Patagonian Continental Sport Fishing General Regulations, text updated on 26 October 2026. Read on 6 November 2026. In dollars, the value changes with the exchange rate of the day."},{"t":"h2","h":"Who does not pay for the permit?"},{"t":"p","h":"No permit fee for people over 65, retirees and pensioners, children up to 12 years old, and people with disabilities with official accreditation (resident category). Residents aged 13 to 17 pay ARS 25,000 for the season."},{"t":"h2","h":"Where is the Patagonian permit valid?"},{"t":"p","h":"Permits issued by Neuquén, Río Negro, Chubut, and the National Parks Administration, with these categories and rates, are the only ones valid for fishing in all waters of those four jurisdictions. Each province also has its own annexes with exceptions by river and lake: check them before fishing a specific water. <strong>Santa Cruz and Tierra del Fuego do not use this permit</strong>: they have their own, with their own rates (see guides for {d:rio-gallegos} and {d:rio-grande})."},{"t":"h2","h":"How long is the permit valid and when is the season?"},{"t":"lista","items":["<strong>Fishing season:</strong> from 1 November 2026 to 1 May 2027 inclusive. Each province's annexes list exceptions (waters that open or close on other dates).","<strong>Season permit:</strong> valid from the date of issue until 31 October 2027.","<strong>One-day and 10-day permits:</strong> valid for the dates indicated on the permit.","<strong>Hours:</strong> fishing is only allowed during daylight hours."]},{"t":"h2","h":"What do I need to bring?"},{"t":"p","h":"The permit is personal and non-transferable, must have all fields completed, and must be carried and shown whenever requested by authorities, along with an identity document. In Chubut, the digital permit managed through the DINO platform can be re-downloaded for free if lost."},{"t":"h2","h":"How much is the permit for a one-week trip?"},{"t":"p","h":"For a foreign angler fishing 6 to 7 days, the 10-day permit (ARS 140,000) is cheaper than six daily permits (ARS 300,000) and less than the season permit (ARS 280,000) if not returning. This is our calculation based on the above rates; the lodge weeks on our price pages state if the license is included: see <a href=\"{n:precio-semana-trucha-patagonia-norte}\">how much a week of trout fishing in Neuquén and Chubut costs</a> and <a href=\"{n:precio-pesca-bariloche-limay}\">a day of fishing in Bariloche</a>."},{"t":"p","h":"<strong>Want help planning your trip?</strong> Write to us using <a href=\"{viaje}\">the trip form</a> and we’ll send you guide and lodge options, free of charge and with no obligation."}]}]}
